## Key equations used in the replication

- **Cost Hamiltonian**: H_C = Σ_i h_i Z_i + Σ_{(i,j)} J_ij Z_i Z_j
- **QAOA ansatz** (Eq. 1--3, generic form):
  |γ,β⟩ = U_B(β_p) U_C(γ_p) ... U_B(β_1) U_C(γ_1) |+⟩^N
  with U_C(γ) = exp(-i γ H_C), U_B(β) = exp(-i β Σ_i X_i)
- **Energy expectation** (Eq. 12): E_p(γ,β) = ⟨γ,β| H_C |γ,β⟩
- **Ratio metric r** (Eq. 16): r = (E_p - E_max) / (E_min - E_max), r ∈ [0,1]
- **Triangle-free p=1 analytic energy** (Eq. 19): closed-form expression
  giving ⟨H_C⟩ as a sum over edges and vertices in terms of cos(2β), sin(2β),
  sin(2γ h_i), etc. (see paper Eq. 19 and our `analytic_E_p1` implementation
  in `work/qaoa_core.py` for the exact form).
- **Linear-annealing initialization** (Eqs. 29--31): γ_k = k/p · Δτ · s,
  β_k = (1 - k/p) · Δτ · s, mimicking a Trotterized quantum-annealing schedule
  used as a warm start for large-p Nelder-Mead refinement.

